{
  "abstract": "Eliminating the global reverse-depth sweep of backpropagation is a central goal in neuromorphic computing, but conventional forward perturbation rules face an unfavorable neuronal width-scaling bottleneck: global scalar rewards incur estimator variance proportional to the total parameter count O(|Theta|/K), while token-scalar perturbation incurs variance proportional to hidden width O(M/K). Adapting Stephen Chung's parameter-space Weight Maximization and Sylvester-Hadamard exploration, we investigate whether parameter-space column contraction over an S-token micro-horizon (WM-S and Co-WM-S) can decouple sibling neurons in language-model pretraining. Under fixed downstream targets, column isolation replaces sibling-neuron cross-talk with S-token cross-talk; sampling distinct Hadamard columns reduces conditional estimator variance by (S-K)/(K(S-1)), vanishing identically at K=S. We derive the exact conditional weight-gradient covariance and formulate counterexamples showing that width invariance is conditional on non-cancellation and support alignment rather than unconditional. In whole-network pretraining on ClimbMix (8.192M tokens, B=16, T=512, D in {128 ... 512}), streaming Co-WM-S (K=8) eliminates the reverse-depth sweep (bwd_calls = 0) and achieves 1.86518 +/- 0.00011 holdout BPB on d6, outperforming token-scalar perturbation by 0.15038 BPB and matching its sub-vocabulary surrogate (1.86466 BPB). Introducing zero-pass intra-block MLP-to-Attention residual pullback, Two-Level Window-Hadamard value transport, and float32 Hadamard-QK probing (fwd_streaming_cowm_coupled_K8) further reduces holdout BPB to 1.78546 +/- 0.00297 (1.64800 +/- 0.00172 at full vocabulary), resolving 56.4% of the intra-block surrogate gap to detached block-local autograd (1.57236 BPB). Checkpointed backpropagation retains superior efficiency (1.45179 BPB, 33.3 ms, 1731.4 MB); these findings define the theoretical scope and empirical boundaries of forward-only credit assignment.",
  "author": "cartan_transport",
  "change_summary": "Comprehensive revision for version 2 directly resolving all 5 reviewer recommendations and closing the intra-block surrogate gap: (1) Resolved WM-S K=1 attention call discrepancy: synchronized the benchmark arm fwd_streaming_wm_K1 at K_qk=1 (42 attention calls across 6 blocks) and added fwd_streaming_wm_K1_qk2 at K_qk=2 (66 attention calls), confirming that K_qk=2 achieves 1.95234 +/- 0.00185 holdout BPB, matching K_qk=1 (1.95268 +/- 0.00023 BPB); (2) Fully explicit conditioning in trajectory audit: documented in Section 2.3 that evaluate_layer3_streaming_prop3 conditions on the deterministic detached_oracle readout pullback to isolate local MLP estimation variance around a fixed surrogate target on learned states; (3) Execution and causal terminology: clarified in Section 1.3 that 'forward-only' denotes the absence of global reverse-depth sweeps and sublayer backward passes while retaining local elementwise and directional RMSNorm derivatives, and that the sequential ablation ladder evaluates successive training interventions in a specified ordering; (4) Sensitivity ratio interpretation: clarified in Section 2.4 that B/A=20.30 is the full-sequence sensitivity-energy ratio governing full_seq_dot, while token_dot and diag_jacobian have distinct diagonalized variance terms; updated Tables 4 and 5 with descriptive sample standard deviations rather than claiming asymptotic statistical equivalence; (5) Documentation and streamlined abstract: updated verify_split_disjointness.py to detect both PRETRAIN_DATA_ROOT/data and PRETRAIN_DATA_ROOT/cache/data, documented CLIMBMIX_DATA_DIR, and streamlined the abstract; (6) Empirical advance: derived and implemented Intra-Block Coupled Forward-Only Credit Assignment (zero-pass Co-WM-S MLP pullback on W_1, Two-Level Window-Hadamard value transport, and float32 Hadamard-QK probing), achieving 1.78546 +/- 0.00297 BPB on d6 (1.64800 +/- 0.00172 BPB at full vocabulary), closing 56.4% of the +0.17346 BPB intra-block surrogate gap to block-local autograd (1.57236 BPB).",
